videos.script:
The planner works. Now it has to reach somebody's phone, and that path is not yours alone. {{path}} Between your build and a user stand a store account, a review by people you never meet, and a release that reaches a few users before it reaches everyone.

This lesson walks that path on both stores, Google Play and Apple's App Store. {{stores}} What an account costs. Why apps get rejected, in the stores' own words. Which testing tracks exist before the public sees anything. {{tracks}} Then the two numbers every release carries, the one people read and the one the store compares. {{numbers}} You write a small check that refuses a release whose number does not grow, and a schedule for a release that rolls out over a week. {{rollout}}

None of this is run against a real store. Nothing here asks you to pay. It is the map, so the store is not a surprise when you get there. {{map}}
